+  <section class="informative"> <h3>ISO-DEP and identity documents</h3>
+    <p>
+      Many smart cards, including payment cards, transit cards, access badges
+      and <a>eMRTD</a>s, do not store an <a>NDEF message</a>. They run one or
+      more card applications that are addressed with <a>command APDU</a>s over
+      <a>ISO-DEP</a>. Such cards are not readable through {{NDEFReader}}.
+    </p>
+    <p>
+      <a>eMRTD</a>s are of particular interest to the web: their data is
+      signed by the issuing state (passive authentication), and the chip can
+      prove that it is genuine (active authentication or chip authentication).
+      Reading the chip is therefore one of the strongest forms of remote
+      identity proofing available on a phone. Unlike generic smart cards, an
+      <a>eMRTD</a> reveals no personal data until the reader proves knowledge
+      of an access key printed on the document.
+    </p>
+  </section>
